FilmCraft is an open source, non-linear video editor for editing, color
grading and sound, written in pure Rust by the ArtCraft team.  It has
bins, Source and Program monitors, a multi-track timeline with ripple,
roll, slip and slide edits, color correction with scopes, keyframed
effects and motion, titles and captions, and audio mixing with loudness
meters.

It carries no FFmpeg: the codecs and containers are its own Rust code,
implemented from the published specifications.  It decodes H.264, HEVC,
VP8, VP9, AV1, ProRes, DNxHD/DNxHR, AAC and Opus, imports MP4/MOV,
Matroska and WebM, AVI, MXF, MPEG transport and program streams and
image sequences, and exports H.264, ProRes, DNxHR, PNG sequences and
animated GIF.

Every action in the user interface is also an engine command, which the
filmcraft-cli tool and its MCP server expose for scripting and agents.
